The portable C in the scenario editor-lines: what it is expected to show
otherwise than the original. A patch of harness/goldens/editor-lines.txt, see
harness/goldens.py: a line with - is the golden's, a line with + is what is
expected in its place.
Deviation: 14, 25 of src/portable_c/DEVIATIONS.md
Why: the Advanced options have no Quick execute commands (14): Clear keyboard
buffer and what is below it in the box stand a row further up, the cursor with
them where it is on that box, the box is a row shorter, and the two rows that
its last row and the shadow below it were on show what is behind the box, the
upper one in the shadow; and the editor reaches every line of the text (25):
where the original stops at the 65,536th line and calls it 0, the portable C
goes on, to the 105,946th with Shift+F7 and to the last with Ctrl+End and
Ctrl+PgDn, shows the line that zebra or the end is on, and the status line has
the number of the line, 105,946 and 105,947 in six cells, with Col and the
column a cell further on; back at line 1 the line is the original's again

